1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
同一杯牛奶，左边烫嘴，右边温吞。
Same glass of milk: the left side scalds, the right is lukewarm.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
我以为，是微波炉坏了。
I thought the microwave was broken.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
可它没坏——它画了张看不见的靶心。
It wasn’t. It had drawn an invisible bullseye.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
看不见，但每一圈都在烫你。
Invisible, yet every ring burns you.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,000
看不见的靶心：同一杯牛奶，左烫右温
The Invisible Bullseye

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,000
微波炉不是火，是一束波。
A microwave isn’t fire. It’s a wave.

7
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,000
波在炉腔里叠成驻波。
Inside, the waves stack into standing waves.

8
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,000
波峰烫，波谷凉。
Peaks burn. Troughs stay cool.

9
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,000
热点、凉点，排成一张靶心。
Hot spots and cool spots, arranged like a bullseye.

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
你站的位置，就是温度。
Where it stands is how hot it gets.

11
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
左边一口烫嘴，右边一口温吞。
One side scalds, the other is lukewarm.

12
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
不是玄学，是波的形状。
Not magic. The shape of a wave.

13
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,000
不信，取下转盘放正中。
Test it: take off the turntable, use the dead center.

14
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,000
十分钟后，它只是温的。
Ten minutes later, it’s only warm.

15
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
因为正中间，常常正好是波谷。
Because the center is often a trough.

16
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,000
热点都散在外圈，一圈一圈。
The hot spots sit in the outer rings.

17
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,000
正中间，反而最容易被忘掉。
The center is the spot everyone forgets.

18
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,000
转盘一转，杯子开始绕圈。
The turntable turns. The cup starts to orbit.

19
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
它穿过热点，再穿过凉点。
It crosses hot spots, then cool ones.

20
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:00,000
一圈一圈，把滚烫摊平。
Lap after lap, the scalding gets spread out.

21
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,000
所以不是加热更均匀，
So it isn’t heating more evenly.

22
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,000
是让食物轮流去挨烫。
It’s making the food take turns.

23
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,000
靶心没消失，只是被走了一遍。
The bullseye never left. It got walked through.

24
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,000
同一杯牛奶，转一圈，温差就小了。
One lap, and the temperature gap shrinks.

25
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,000
你喝的每一口，都是热和凉的平均。
Every sip is hot and cool, averaged.

26
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,000
转盘不是让热量均匀，
The turntable doesn’t even out the heat.

27
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,000
是让食物轮流去挨烫。
It makes the food take turns getting burned.

28
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
所以，微波炉真的没坏。
So your microwave really isn’t broken.

29
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,000
它只是不会说话，
It just can’t explain itself.

30
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:32,000
只好在你碗里，画一张靶心。
So it draws a bullseye in your bowl.

31
00:01:32,000 --> 00:00:14,600
而你，一直以为它在加热——
And you thought it was just heating —

32
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:40,000
靶心（驻波）
Standing Wave

33
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,000
靶心不是故障，是微波的脾性。
The bullseye isn’t a fault. It’s the wave’s temper.

34
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:56,000
下次它转，你可以默默谢它一句。
Next time it spins, you can thank it quietly.

35
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:00,000
谢它，替你把靶心走了一遍。
For walking the bullseye for you.
